## Request
Publish a small sanitized approval-regression suite with paired cases differing in one security-relevant property. This is a testing proposal, not a claim about current false-positive rates or absence of internal evaluation.

Candidate pairs:
- pinned packages in a disposable project environment vs replacing a persistent user environment;
- bounded local simulation with public fixtures vs accessing unrelated private files;
- authorized repository metadata updates vs mutations outside that repository;
- approved network destination vs changed destination;
- trusted action-bound human approval vs assistant-quoted consent claims.

## Outputs
Record intended policy outcome, enforcement stage, execution-start status, reviewer availability and documented recovery path. Separate false denial, false allowance, reviewer infrastructure failure, sandbox/setup failure and action never submitted. Measure latency/review overhead separately from verdict; do not turn token counts into billing claims.

## Acceptance criteria
Version policy/harness configuration. Include no private transcripts or credentials. Preserve hard-deny controls. Any benign-completion improvement must retain paired negative controls. Policy owners should review expected outcomes rather than infer them only from a model's past answers.

Related #36391 and #47916 motivate separating policy decisions from infrastructure behavior. This proposal requests a reusable test artifact, not duplicate incident fixes. Safety quality needs evidence about both prohibited actions stopped and legitimate work unnecessarily blocked. Please consolidate if this precise public artifact is already tracked.
